+# Auth journey findings on supremeai-studio.pages.dev (passkey 405 live; silent 401; mixed-language error copy)
+
+- **Agent**: human-eye (Job 478633, cycle-19, 2026-10-29T00:57+08)
+- **Bundle under test**: `Build 2026-10-27T18:10:28.851Z` (verified client-side on /login)
+- **Companion report**: human-eye-health-staleness-20261029.md (H-1)
+
+## F-1a — Passkey flow hits same-origin Pages host → 405 (STILL LIVE, structural)
+
+Reproduced live (Playwright browser, 2026-10-28 ~17:00Z):
+
+```
+POST https://supremeai-studio.pages.dev/api/auth/passkey/login/options → 405
+```
+
+- No Cloudflare Pages Function exists for `/api/auth/*` on the pages.dev host, so the
+  request 405s at the edge.
+- Working API calls correctly target `https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com`
+  (e.g. `POST /api/v1/auth/login`, `GET /api/health-aggregation → 200`), so only the
+  passkey path uses the wrong base URL.
+- UI impact: a vague alert renders — "Failed to initialize biometric login" — and the
+  passkey button stays unusable. Root cause unchanged from the earlier human-eye report
+  (F-1): auth base-URL mismatch for the passkey flow.
+
+**Smallest safe fix**: point the passkey options/verify calls at the configured API base
+(`VITE_API_BASE`/existing token constant used by `/api/v1/*`) or implement a Pages
+Function/Worker proxy for `/api/auth/*`. No UI redesign; reuse existing apiClient.
+
+**Regression test**: vitest — mock fetch; assert passkey init requests use the API base
+origin; component test — mock 405 → alert text renders.
+
+## F-7 — Invalid-credentials 401 produces NO user-visible error (WCAG 3.3.1 A)
+
+Reproduced (warm API): submit `human-eye-qa@example.com` / `WrongPass123!` →
+
+```
+OPTIONS /api/v1/auth/login → 200 (preflight ok)
+POST    /api/v1/auth/login → 401
+```
+
+Post-response UI: button returns to "Sign in"; **no toast, no inline error, no text
+anywhere** (full accessibility-tree scan + `body.innerText` tail captured; screenshot
+`c19-login-401-no-error.png`). Console logs `Login failed: TypeError/401` only.
+WCAG 3.3.1 (Error Identification, Level A) requires errors that are automatically detected
+to be identified and described in text.
+
+Note (related, cold-start): during a Render wake window the first attempts fail as
+`OPTIONS → 400` + `TypeError: Failed to fetch`; the apiClient auto-retry recovered
+(observed 400→retry→200 preflight→401). The recovery is good, but during failure windows
+the user gets zero feedback as well.
+
+**Smallest safe fix**: on login promise rejection, render the existing shared
+error/alert component (the one used for "Failed to initialize biometric login") inside the
+form with role=alert; map 401 → "Incorrect email or password.", network errors →
+"Network problem — check your connection." Use existing tokens/components; no new patterns.
+
+**Regression test**: component test — mock 401 ⇒ `[role=alert]` visible with mapped copy;
+mock network failure ⇒ retry + mapped copy; assert focus management stays in the form.
+
+## F-8 — Mixed-language error copy on an English product
+
+- `/register` empty-submit alert: **"দয়া করে সব ফিল্ড পূরণ করুন।"** (Bengali) on an
+  otherwise all-English flow (verified via accessibility tree; `role=alert` present — good).
+- Earlier the same day, transient page-level error rendered Chinese:
+  "Error 408 请求超时，请稍后重试" (observed 11:57+08; did not reproduce later).
+- Strings appear hardcoded per-component instead of routed through one i18n/message layer.
+
+**Smallest safe fix**: route these messages through the existing message-constant module
+with English defaults (or locale-aware lookup); replace the two hardcoded strings.
+
+**Regression test**: grep-style lint test asserting register/login components contain no
+non-ASCII literal user-facing strings outside the i18n module; component test renders
+alerts and asserts locale of copy.
+
+## PASS evidence (same session, same environment)
+
+- `/register` journey: renders Full name/Email/Password/Confirm; "Create one" → `/register`
+  (href verified); validation alert announced via `role=alert`.
+- Keyboard: Tab order logical (home → fields → buttons); visible focus indicator
+  (outline solid 2px) on inputs and buttons.
+- Mobile 375×812: login renders completely; screenshot `c19-mobile-login.png`.
+- FCP (Performance API, 3 fresh navigations, headless Chromium, warm CDN):
+  144 / 204 / 120 ms (median ≈144 ms) — meets the <1.0s target **in this environment**;
+  no Lighthouse score claimed. TTFB 28–33 ms.
+- `devtools_audit` (HTTP-fallback mode): 200 in 99ms; HSTS/CSP/XFO/XCTO all present.
+  Browser-audit path of the tool remains unavailable (degraded), so browser evidence here
+  was collected locally with Playwright-equivalent tooling.
+- Console: non-fatal self-healing warnings only (`[Config] … safe defaults`,
+  `[Self-Healing] CONFIG_FETCH_FAILED`); no uncaught page errors.
+
+## Why
+
+All three defects sit on the single most important journey (first login / first account).
+F-1a blocks a advertised auth method; F-7 leaves the primary error state invisible (A-level
+WCAG); F-8 confuses users with wrong-locale copy. Fixes are string/base-URL-level — no
+redesign, existing design tokens and components only.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+- **Rebuild login as a modal or new flow**: unnecessary redesign; defects are call-target
+  and error-rendering level.
+- **Global toast system for F-7**: new pattern; the page already has an alert component
+  that screen readers announce — reuse it inline instead.
+- **Silently retrying passkey init against pages.dev forever**: masks a 404/405 route bug;
+  fix the base URL, keep one visible failure path.
+- **Auto-translating all strings at runtime**: out of scope; the i18n layer already
+  exists — route constants through it.
